{"name":"Tokyo Underground","hex":"#ecf3d8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"underground","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Below the ground; below the surface of the Earth.","Hidden, furtive, secretive."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Below the ground.","Secretly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underground"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tokyo Underground","blocks":[{"text":"Tokyo Underground  is a Japanese manga series by Akinobu Uraku and published by Square Enix. It was adapted into an anime television series by Pierrot and directed by Hayato Date. It was broadcast on TV Tokyo from April to September 2002. The anime series was released on DVD by Geneon Entertainment in North America and released by Manga Entertainment in the UK and by Tokyo Night Train in Australia. It aired in Canada on the digital channel G4techTV, starting on July 22, 2007. It was also aired on ABS-CBN and Hero TV in the Philippines and Adult Swim in Australia."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7b/Tokyo_Underground_Volume_1_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokyo_Underground","wikidata":"Q710369"},{"title":"Tokyo","blocks":[{"text":"Tokyo, officially the Tokyo Metropolis, is the capital and most populous city of Japan. The population of the city proper was over 14 million as of 2023. The Greater Tokyo Area, which includes Tokyo and parts of six neighboring prefectures, is the third-most populous metropolitan area in the world, with 33 million residents as of 2025."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Skyscrapers_of_Shinjuku_2009_January.jpg/330px-Skyscrapers_of_Shinjuku_2009_January.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokyo","wikidata":"Q1490"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43